    <l n="1" type="heading" level="1" para="true">LIBR. 2. INSTIT. TIT. 24.</l>
    <l n="2" type="heading" level="2" para="true">De singul. rebus per fideic. relictis.</l>
    <l n="3" para="true">Differentia inter legatum &amp; singula-</l>
    <l n="4">re fideicommissum proponitur.</l>
    <l n="5" para="true">§. 1.</l>
    <l n="6">1. Quae res restitutionis onere graventur?</l>
    <l n="7">2. Quis possit gravari?</l>
    <l n="8" para="true">§. 2.</l>
    <l n="9">1. Libertas per fideicommissum relinqui</l>
    <l n="10">potest.</l>
    <l n="11">2. Differentia multiplex inter libertatem</l>
    <l n="12">directam &amp; fideicommissariam.</l>
    <l n="13" para="true">§. 3.</l>
    <l n="14">Quae sint verba fideicommissaria?</l>
    <l n="15" type="heading" level="1" para="true">LIBR. 2. INSTIT. TIT. 25.</l>
    <l n="16" type="heading" level="2" para="true">De Codicillis.</l>
    <l n="17" type="heading" level="3" para="true">In Princ.</l>
    <l n="18">1. Ultimae voluntatis sunt variae species.</l>
    <l n="19">2. Definiantur codicilli.</l>
    <l n="20">3. Quo sensu codicilli ad Lentuli aetatem</l>
    <l n="21">referantur?</l>
    <l n="22">4. Ad Principis exemplum subjecti respi-</l>
    <l n="23">ciunt.</l>
    <l n="24">5 Princeps sapientes in consilium adhibet.</l>
    <l n="25">6. Suadetur aliquid à justo, necessario &amp; utili.</l>
    <l n="26">7. Quis possit facere codicillos?</l>
    <l n="27" para="true">§. 1.</l>
    <l n="28">1. Quot generum sint codicilli?</l>
    <l n="29">2. An confirmandi per testamentum posterius?</l>
    <l n="30">2. Particula nam explicatur.</l>
    <l n="31" type="heading" level="3" para="true">§. 3.</l>
    <l n="32" para="true">1. Codicilli nullam fere solemnitatem</l>
    <l n="33">desiderant.</l>
    <l n="34" para="true">2. Quid moribus?</l>
    <l n="35" type="heading" level="1" para="true">Libr. 3. Instit. Tit. 1.</l>
    <l n="36" type="heading" level="2" para="true">De Hared. qua ab intest. deferuntur.</l>
    <l n="37" para="true">1. Causa testati potior est causa intestati.</l>
    <l n="38" para="true">2. Hac tamen sape equior est.</l>
    <l n="39" para="true">3. Successio juris antiqui &amp; medii delineatur.</l>
    <l n="40" para="true">4. Successionis modi proponuntur.</l>
    <l n="41" para="true">5. Generalia circa successionem juris no-</l>
    <l n="42">vissimi traduntur.</l>
    <l n="43" para="true">6. Ipsa successio descendentium explicatur.</l>
    <l n="44" para="true">7. Quid moribus?</l>
    <l n="45" para="true">8. Qua successio ascendentium?</l>
    <l n="46" para="true">9. Qua collateralium?</l>
    <l n="47" para="true">10. Quid moribus?</l>
    <l n="48" para="true">11. De successione conjugum?</l>
    <l n="49" para="true">12. Quid moribus?</l>
    <l n="50" para="true">13. De socio liberalitatis imperialis,</l>
    <l n="51">&amp; collegiis, deque successione fisci.</l>
    <l n="52" para="true">14. Quid moribus?</l>
    <l n="53" para="true">15. Generalis feudorum successio.</l>
    <l n="54" para="true">16. Describitur successio juris Hebraeorum.</l>
    <l n="55" type="heading" level="3" para="true">In Princ.</l>
    <l n="56" para="true">
      <i>Quot modis quis dica-</i>
    </l>
    <l n="57">
      <i>tur intestatus?</i>
    </l>
    <l n="58" type="heading" level="3" para="true">§. 1.</l>
    <l n="59" para="true">
      <i>Sui ex 12. tabulis positivè non vocantur.</i>
    </l>
    <l n="60" type="heading" level="3" para="true">§. 2.</l>
    <l n="61" para="true">
      <i>Quinam dicantur sui?</i>
    </l>
    <l n="62" type="heading" level="3" para="true">§. 3.</l>
    <l n="63" type="foot" para="true">1. Codicilli multum à testamento distinguuntur.</l>
  </main_text>
